[gd_scene load_steps=22 format=3]

; DEVELOPMENT SCENE — not a world module, not contract-conforming, not
; discovered by the hub. It exists so the core systems can be seen running
; inside a real _physics_process instead of only inside the test harness.
; The reference template (REQ-029) is the contract-conforming starting point a
; contributor copies; this is the developers' proving ground and is superseded
; the moment the template lands.
;
; LAYOUT, and what each piece is for. Spawn is the origin. Godot's forward is
; -Z, so W walks you toward the ramp, the climb wall and the tunnel; the pool is
; BEHIND spawn, across the ground's far edge at z=6. The camera trails the
; direction of travel, so backing into the water turns the view around with you.
;
;   Ground      z -30..6,  top y=0     the land grammar
;   Pool        z 6..30,   floor y=-12  the pit the water fills
;   Water       z 6..30,   y -12..0     the water grammar; its surface is FLUSH
;                                       with the ground so the transition is a
;                                       step off the edge, not a fall through air
;   Ramp        x -14      15 degrees   a slope the waddle has to climb
;   ClimbWall   x 14       y 0..12      physics layer 4 AND group "climbable",
;                                       so both routes ClimbSurface accepts are
;                                       live; taller than climb.max_height_m
;                                       (6 m) on purpose, so the ceiling is
;                                       observable rather than theoretical
;   ClimbLedge  y 12..13                what the wall gets you to
;   Anchor      (-8, 6, 2)              inside grapple.max_range_m (12 m) of
;                                       spawn, in group "grapple_anchor"
;   TunnelRoof  (8, 3.5, -4)            low cover, to see the camera's collision
;                                       pull-in fire

